content.thinking:
Now I see the full picture:

**`img-auto-cover` mixin**:
```scss
@mixin img-auto-cover($percent: 56.25%) {
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
  height: 0;
  padding-bottom: $percent;

  img {
    @include pos-full();  // likely position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%
  }
}


```

So the `img` element gets positioned absolutely within the container created by `img-auto-cover`, but `video` elements don't get that treatment automatically—they need the `img-cover` mixin applied separately to handle their sizing.

```
Still writing styles...
```

The issue is that the `<figure>` uses the padding-bottom trick to maintain aspect ratio, giving it zero intrinsic height, so a child with `height: 100%` would collapse to 0px. The `<img>` avoids this because it gets absolute positioning from the `img-auto-cover` mixin, but the `<video>` only gets the cover styles without the positioning, causing it to fail. I need to add `position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0;` to the video to fix this. I'm realizing that `img-auto-cover` already applies the absolute positioning to `img` elements, so they're covered. For `video`, I just need to add that same absolute positioning with the `pos-full` mixin to make it display properly alongside the image styling.

